    {
      "id": "PRE-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-progression-relative-error",
      "title": "The exceptional scale in the corrected prime density and in the weighted error",
      "equations": [
        "inputs-progression-exceptional-scale",
        "inputs-progression-weighted-saving"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "EZS-02"
      ],
      "hypotheses": "8 divides the positive modulus m, a is prime to m, and log t ≥ C log m log(log m+2) in the weighted estimate. For the elementary main-term bound U≥16 and log U≥log m. The exceptional pair, when present, has the range and sign stated in the progression theorem.",
      "statement": "The corrected main term dominates Uη/(2φ(m) log U). The explicit formula with zero density and repulsion supplies an error for the progression Chebyshev sum containing the same factor η. The range absorbs the logarithmic loss in the weighted zero sum.",
